Subject: [PATCH] POSIX memory: a commit checks its range with msync, not /proc/self/maps

AllocFixed's commit on an existing reservation (the EEXIST path) read and parsed /proc/self/maps to check the
range is mapped: about 0.2 ms per commit with some 1,150 mappings. King Kong commits guest pages one at a time
(300 in a row at one spot of Skull Island coast, over 1,000 a second while a chapter loads), so the game
stalled for 80 ms there on Linux (ROG Ally, every pass of the benchmark route at a 16:9 picture).
msync(MS_ASYNC) fails with ENOMEM where any page is unmapped and does nothing else.
---
--- a/src/core/memory_posix.cpp	2026-10-30 11:22:16.697240200 +0000
+++ b/src/core/memory_posix.cpp	2026-10-30 11:32:52.729573100 +0000
@@ -200,25 +200,12 @@
     return false;
   }
 
-  std::ifstream maps("/proc/self/maps");
-  if (!maps.is_open())
-    return false;
-
-  uintptr_t cursor = begin;
-  std::string line;
-  while (std::getline(maps, line)) {
-    LinuxMapEntry e;
-    if (!ParseProcMapsLine(line, e))
-      continue;
-    if (e.end <= cursor)
-      continue;
-    if (e.start > cursor)
-      return false;  // gap found
-    cursor = e.end;
-    if (cursor >= end)
-      return true;
-  }
-  return cursor >= end;
+  // msync with MS_ASYNC fails with ENOMEM where any page of the range is not mapped and does nothing else. It
+  // replaces reading /proc/self/maps, which took about 0.2 ms on every commit: a game committing 300 pages one
+  // by one stalled for 80 ms (King Kong, ROG Ally).
+  const uintptr_t page = static_cast<uintptr_t>(sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE));
+  const uintptr_t aligned = begin & ~(page - 1);
+  return msync(reinterpret_cast<void*>(aligned), end - aligned, MS_ASYNC) == 0;
 }
 
 // Convert /proc/self/maps permission chars to PageAccess
